  },
  {
   "id": "dn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1390,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 32,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100072,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700504,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Vector wins on the requirement that matters most - 'data and battery frugality' - because vector tiles are 5-10x SMALLER, the\nsingle largest bandwidth saving available in the product.",
   "originalText": "Vector wins on the requirement that matters most - 'data and battery frugality' - because vector tiles are 5-10x SMALLER, the\nsingle largest bandwidth saving available in the product.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1436,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 81,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100073,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700511,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "But the easily-overlooked benefit is arguably bigger: ONE TILE SET SERVES EVERY STYLE AND EVERY LANGUAGE. Dark mode, satellite\noverlay, transit emphasis, high-contrast accessibility and 80 languages of labels are all CLIENT-SIDE STYLE RULES applied to\nthe same geometry. Under raster tiling, each of those would be a separate 60 PB TILE SET. So vector tiles do not just save\nbandwidth - they avoid multiplying the largest dataset in the system by the number of visual variants, which is what makes\nthose variants economically possible at all.",
   "originalText": "But the easily-overlooked benefit is arguably bigger: ONE TILE SET SERVES EVERY STYLE AND EVERY LANGUAGE. Dark mode, satellite\noverlay, transit emphasis, high-contrast accessibility and 80 languages of labels are all CLIENT-SIDE STYLE RULES applied to\nthe same geometry. Under raster tiling, each of those would be a separate 60 PB TILE SET. So vector tiles do not just save\nbandwidth - they avoid multiplying the largest dataset in the system by the number of visual variants, which is what makes\nthose variants economically possible at all.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "dn3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1546,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#b45309",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100074,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700518,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The genuine cost is client CPU, and it partially fights the requirement it serves: you save RADIO energy and spend GPU energy.\nOn modern hardware the radio dominates so the trade is clearly favourable - but it is a real trade rather than a free win, and\nit means very old devices get a worse experience.",
   "originalText": "The genuine cost is client CPU, and it partially fights the requirement it serves: you save RADIO energy and spend GPU energy.\nOn modern hardware the radio dominates so the trade is clearly favourable - but it is a real trade rather than a free win, and\nit means very old devices get a worse experience.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
