   "originalText": "(21, 300000, 400000) -+\n(21, 300001, 400000) -+->  hash 3f8a...  ->  ONE stored object\n(21, 300002, 400000) -+",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "dd",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "e1n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 760,
   "y": 1704,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 75,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100080,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700560,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "At zoom 21 a tile covering open Pacific contains NOTHING - and so do the billions\naround it. They are byte-identical, so tiles are content-addressed: hash the\nbytes, store one copy per distinct hash, map (z,x,y) -> hash. It also improves\nthe CDN, because a single hot ocean tile is cached once per edge instead of being\nbillions of distinct COLD objects.",
   "originalText": "At zoom 21 a tile covering open Pacific contains NOTHING - and so do the billions\naround it. They are byte-identical, so tiles are content-addressed: hash the\nbytes, store one copy per distinct hash, map (z,x,y) -> hash. It also improves\nthe CDN, because a single hot ocean tile is cached once per edge instead of being\nbillions of distinct COLD objects.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "e2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1802,
   "width": 377,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100081,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700567,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "2   don't precompute every level everywhere",
   "originalText": "2   don't precompute every level everywhere",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "e2n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1828,
   "width": 934,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100082,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700574,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Zoom 21 is only meaningful where there is detail to show. Dense cities are generated to 21; open ocean stops at maybe zoom 8,\nbecause there is nothing further to reveal. Requests below the generated depth upscale the deepest available tile -\nimperceptible when the content is featureless. So the tile set is DEEP WHERE INFORMATION DENSITY IS HIGH AND SHALLOW\nELSEWHERE, which is the same density-adaptive principle a quadtree applies to point data, here applied to storage depth.",
   "originalText": "Zoom 21 is only meaningful where there is detail to show. Dense cities are generated to 21; open ocean stops at maybe zoom 8,\nbecause there is nothing further to reveal. Requests below the generated depth upscale the deepest available tile -\nimperceptible when the content is featureless. So the tile set is DEEP WHERE INFORMATION DENSITY IS HIGH AND SHALLOW\nELSEWHERE, which is the same density-adaptive principle a quadtree applies to point data, here applied to storage depth.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "e3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1918,
   "width": 238,
   "height": 17,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100083,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700581,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "3   let the CDN do the work",
   "originalText": "3   let the CDN do the work",
   "fontSize": 14,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "cdn",
   "type": "rectangle",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 1946,
   "width": 700,
   "height": 74,
   "strokeColor": "#1e293b",
   "backgroundColor": "#1e293b",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 2,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100084,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700588,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": [
    {
     "id": "cdn_t",
     "type": "text"
    }
   ],
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "roundness": {
    "type": 3
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "cdn_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 1960,
   "width": 684,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100085,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700595,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "client  ->  CDN edge (nearest PoP)\n   HIT  (~99%)  ->  served locally, origin never involved\n   MISS ( ~1%)  ->  fetch from object-storage origin, cache, serve",
   "originalText": "client  ->  CDN edge (nearest PoP)\n   HIT  (~99%)  ->  served locally, origin never involved\n   MISS ( ~1%)  ->  fetch from object-storage origin, cache, serve",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "cdn",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "e3n",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 760,
   "y": 1946,
   "width": 614,
   "height": 45,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100086,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700602,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The ~99% hit rate holds because tile requests are extremely concentrated - cities,\nmotorways, tourist destinations - and immutability lets an edge cache a tile\nINDEFINITELY with Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable.",
   "originalText": "The ~99% hit rate holds because tile requests are extremely concentrated - cities,\nmotorways, tourist destinations - and immutability lets an edge cache a tile\nINDEFINITELY with Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "e3n2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 760,
   "y": 2012,
   "width": 606,
   "height": 105,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100087,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700609,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Two CDN behaviours are load-bearing. REQUEST COLLAPSING turns concurrent edge\nmisses for the same key into ONE origin fetch - without it, a suddenly-popular\nlocation delivers thousands of identical origin requests at once, a thundering\nherd on a per-object basis. And PREFETCHING ADJACENT TILES buys the perception of\nan instantly-responsive map at the cost of bandwidth for tiles that may go\nunused, which on a metered connection is a genuine trade - so it is usually tuned\nby connection type.",
   "originalText": "Two CDN behaviours are load-bearing. REQUEST COLLAPSING turns concurrent edge\nmisses for the same key into ONE origin fetch - without it, a suddenly-popular\nlocation delivers thousands of identical origin requests at once, a thundering\nherd on a per-object basis. And PREFETCHING ADJACENT TILES buys the perception of\nan instantly-responsive map at the cost of bandwidth for tiles that may go\nunused, which on a metered connection is a genuine trade - so it is usually tuned\nby connection type.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "d6",
   "type": "line",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 2130,
   "width": 1680,
   "height": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#cbd5e1",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
